# The game popup scrolled (source/ui/ui_popup.c) on Recent's first game,
# whose 8 items show 7 rows: each step lands whole in one frame (the rows
# that stay move in VRAM; the incoming row, the highlights and the bar are
# drawn), down past the last row, then UP from the first item to the last
# (a jump of two rows). Every frame is hashed: a half-drawn one fails.
#! settings 28=1
-w "nav: home ready"
-k @8:A -k @12:-
-w "nav: page recent ready"
-k @8:START -k @12:-
-w "screen ready: game-popup"
-s @30:open.png
-k @40:DOWN -k @44:- -k @52:DOWN -k @56:- -k @64:DOWN -k @68:- -k @76:DOWN -k @80:-
-k @88:DOWN -k @92:- -k @100:DOWN -k @104:- -k @112:DOWN -k @116:-
-s @124:bottom.png
-k @130:DOWN -k @134:-
-s @146:top.png
-k @150:UP -k @154:-
-s @166:wrapped.png
-H @38:@166
